+# Ledger verify contract (Crumbline)
+
+Subject: how Synapse re-verifies a ledger from `crumbs::ledger::Ledger::verify(genesis, records)` in aien-sovereign-core.
+
+Source: agent beta (aien-sovereign-core), reply [A1] relayed by the orchestrator at 2026-10-16T13:05:58Z. Synapse has not read the implementation; this is beta's description only.
+
+Quoted answer:
+
+> For an empty record slice, Ledger::verify returns Ok with the genesis digest passed in, since the loop never runs and the starting head is returned unchanged. If the chain is broken, meaning a record's prev_root does not match the running head or its recomputed root does not match its stored root, it returns Err(LedgerError::Chain) at the first bad record and stops checking. On success for a non-empty slice, it returns Ok with the root of the last record.
+
+What Synapse can rely on:
+
+- Empty slice: Ok(genesis), not an error.
+- Broken chain: Err(LedgerError::Chain), at the first bad record.
+- Valid non-empty slice: Ok(root of last record).
+
+Open: exact field names and digest type are not confirmed.
